WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:09.683
A monitor watches a payments node, which sends a heartbeat every second: a tiny message saying it's alive.

2
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.818
The monitor measures silence, the time since the last heartbeat.

3
00:00:13.818 --> 00:00:16.633
It climbs, and drops to zero when one arrives.

4
00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:22.801
The simplest detector is a fixed timeout: silence past 1.5 seconds means dead.

5
00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:27.627
On a calm network the gaps stay near one second, and it never fires.

6
00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:32.353
Across regions, each heartbeat takes 30 to 830 milliseconds.

7
00:00:32.353 --> 00:00:38.983
The gaps spread out, some pass 1.5 seconds, and each is a false alarm about a live node.

8
00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:42.657
Raise the timeout to 3 seconds and the alarms stop.

9
00:00:42.657 --> 00:00:48.268
But a real crash now takes 3 seconds to notice, twice what the calm network needs.

10
00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.293
The phi accrual detector lets history choose.

11
00:00:51.293 --> 00:00:57.888
It fits a bell curve to the last thousand gaps, and asks how likely a healthy node is to stay this quiet.

12
00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:03.279
Phi is that chance on a log scale: phi 8 means one in a hundred million.

13
00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:06.827
On this link it passes 8 after about 2.8 seconds.

14
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.416
On the calm network it passes 8 after about 1.6.

15
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:14.151
Each link gets its own timeout, from its own history.

16
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:17.891
Every detector so far asks whether the node answers.

17
00:01:17.891 --> 00:01:23.776
Now its database pool jams: all 20 connections are stuck, and every payment times out.

18
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.207
The heartbeats come from a thread that never touches the database, so phi stays low.

19
00:01:29.207 --> 00:01:32.555
The monitor sees a healthy node, and users see errors.

20
00:01:32.555 --> 00:01:33.919
That's a gray failure.

21
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:43.024
So test health with real work: a synthetic payment through the whole path, or a proxy that stops routing to an instance whose requests fail.

22
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:45.148
A detector can only suspect.

23
00:01:45.148 --> 00:01:50.415
Let history set the timeout, and let real requests decide what healthy means.
